From: DKR-R Windows 95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Say what the processor is doing in each silence

Patch 0042 found no guest thread running for 48% of the wall, and could name
only half of it: the renderer's bit, sampled when the silence starts, covered
45% and the rest was "other". The audio microcode is the obvious suspect -- it
runs on the SP task thread, outside every guest thread, so on one processor its
time can only appear as a silence -- and nothing asked it.

The game now exports `dkr_audio_busy` beside `dkr_renderer_busy`, and both are
sampled at the start **and** the end of each silence, which is charged to the
union. One run on the test machine, 75 s, a frame of 123.4 ms:

  [trace][idle-by] neither=2241083 render=10459776 audio=11263068 both=12274423 us

  the renderer only    10.46 s   28.9%
  the audio only       11.26 s   31.1%
  both in progress     12.27 s   33.9%
  neither               2.24 s    6.2%

94% of the silence has the renderer or the audio microcode in progress. The
silence is not waiting; it is the processor, busy on host threads that are
not guest threads.

